    "description": "<h2>Outcome and context</h2><p>Wagertech&#039;s notes flag that manual Player creation is needed, to be scoped as part of a VIP flow. This is a scoping item, not a build yet.</p><h2>Current state</h2><p>BUILD-173 (PL-1, WAGR-160) notes that manual Player/Sign-Up creation, outside the CMS pipeline, is currently restricted to Lina, Jay, Owen, and Emily — but no dedicated manual-creation flow or UI has been scoped or built. Players are otherwise created only via the CMS/SLC intake pipeline.</p><h2>Proposed solution</h2><p>Scope what a manual Player creation flow needs to support as part of the VIP flow work: who can trigger it, what fields are required at creation, how it avoids creating duplicates of CMS-sourced players, and how it fits alongside the existing SLC intake pipeline.</p><h2>Acceptance criteria</h2><ol><li><p>A scoping document or set of follow-on tickets exists describing the manual Player creation flow for VIP players.</p></li><li><p>The scope explicitly addresses duplicate prevention against CMS-created Players.</p></li></ol><h2>Dependencies</h2><p>Related to BUILD-173 — Player: Core Details fields (WAGR-160) and BUILD-230 — Player: Manage Duplicate Player (WAGR-40).</p><h2>Source</h2><p>Wagertech Notes / Questions (Wagertech Notes section), Player record doc, reviewed Sep 2026: &quot;Manual Player Creation Needed (to be scoped in VIP Flow).&quot; https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mp3b1qpJkzKNDztEQpdnv-BYCgUgDdXe5jLuJi-ix1U/edit?tab=t.0</p>",
